==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|myocardial infarct}}

===Etymology===
From Late [[Latin]] [[infarctus]] + [[French]] [[myocarde]] < from Greek [[ἔμφραγμα]] (obstacle) [[του]] (of) [[μυοκάρδιο|μυοκαρδίου]] (heart muscle)

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|cardiology|pathology}} [[necrosis|Necrosis]] of heart muscle caused by an interruption to the supply of [[blood]] to the [[heart]], often as a result of [[coronary thrombosis]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|cardiac infarction}}
* {{l|en|heart attack}}

